# Choose a content type

| If someone needs to... | Write a... | Follow |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Do something now | Label or button | [Write clear titles](../writing-guidelines/clear-titles.html) |
| Understand a field | Hint | [Write clear summaries](../writing-guidelines/summaries.html) |
| Know something happened | Notification | [Content blocks](../formatting-content/content-blocks.html) |
| Know what went wrong | Error message | [States, requests and errors](../writing-guidelines/states-and-errors.html) |
| Fix a problem now | Troubleshooting page | See “Fix a problem now” below |
| Set something up for the first time | Set-up page | [Create a clear structure](../writing-guidelines/clear-structure.html) |
| Learn how to do a task | Help page | [Create a clear structure](../writing-guidelines/clear-structure.html) |

## Fix a problem now

Someone fixing a fault is stressed and short of time. Start with what they see. Then give the confirmed cause, one fix, and what to try next. Keep it to about 7 steps and leave out background.

| Before | After |
| --- | --- |
| Hall light troubleshooting: an overview of Zigbee, pairing and range. | **The hall light does not respond**<br>The hub cannot reach the light.<br>1. Turn the light off and on at the wall.<br>2. Wait 30 seconds. The light should reconnect.<br>If it does not, move the hub closer or pair the light again. |

## Set up for the first time

Start with what the person needs before they begin: the device, the app and how long it takes. Then give the steps. Keep background and options on another page.

<h2 id="wg-090">Record who owns it, where it came from and what it covers</h2>

Every piece of Civica content has an owner, a source and a scope.

| Before | After |
| --- | --- |
| Heating help (no owner, no date) | Heating help. Owner: the Civica maintainers. Source: Home Assistant Core 2026.11 climate documentation. Covers: thermostat and schedule controls only. |
| This guide applies to everything. | This guide applies to Civica labels and help. It does not apply to native Home Assistant screens. |
